#: source/language/builtins.md:427 source/language/builtins.md:456
#: source/language/builtins.md:2737
msgid ""
"Not available in [pure evaluation mode](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-"
"pure-eval)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:436
msgid ""
"Return the [Unix time](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unix_time) at first "
"evaluation. Repeated references to that name re-use the initially obtained "
"value."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:439 source/language/builtins.md:554
#: source/language/builtins.md:569 source/language/builtins.md:597
#: source/language/builtins.md:2112 source/language/builtins.md:2525
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:452
msgid ""
"The [store path](../store/store-path.md) of a derivation depending on "
"`currentTime` differs for each evaluation, unless both evaluate "
"`builtins.currentTime` in the same second."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:465
msgid ""
"This is like `seq e1 e2`, except that _e1_ is evaluated _deeply_: if it’s a "
"list or set, its elements or attributes are also evaluated recursively."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:476
msgid ""
"Return the directory part of the string _s_, that is, everything before the "
"final slash in the string. This is similar to the GNU `dirname` command."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:487
msgid "Return the quotient of the numbers _e1_ and _e2_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:496
msgid ""
"Return `true` if a value equal to _x_ occurs in the list _xs_, and `false` "
"otherwise. Short-circuits and does not evaluate elements that occur in the "
"list after the first match."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:507
msgid ""
"Return element _n_ from the list _xs_. Elements are counted starting from 0. "
"A fatal error occurs if the index is out of bounds."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:517 source/language/builtins.md:2276
#: source/language/builtins.md:3067
msgid "Primitive value."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:519 source/language/builtins.md:3069
msgid ""
"It can be returned by [comparison operators](../language/"
"operators.md#comparison) and used in [conditional expressions](../language/"
"syntax.md#conditionals)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:524
msgid "The name `false` is not special, and can be shadowed:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:540
msgid ""
"This function is only available if the [`fetch-closure` experimental feature]"
"(../development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-fetch-closure) is "
"enabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:542 source/language/builtins.md:886
#: source/language/builtins.md:1505 source/language/builtins.md:1782
#: source/language/builtins.md:2296 source/language/builtins.md:2349
msgid ""
"For example, include the following in [`nix.conf`](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:548
msgid ""
"Fetch a store path [closure](../glossary.md#gloss-closure) from a binary "
"cache, and return the store path as a string with context."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:550
msgid ""
"This function can be invoked in three ways that we will discuss in order of "
"preference."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:552
msgid "**Fetch a content-addressed store path**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:556
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchClosure {\n"
"  fromStore = \"https://cache.nixos.org\";\n"
"  fromPath = /nix/store/ldbhlwhh39wha58rm61bkiiwm6j7211j-git-2.33.1;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:563
msgid ""
"This is the simplest invocation, and it does not require the user of the "
"expression to configure [`trusted-public-keys`](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-trusted-public-keys) to ensure their authenticity."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:565
msgid ""
"If your store path is [input addressed](../glossary.md#gloss-input-addressed-"
"store-object) instead of content addressed, consider the other two "
"invocations."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:567
msgid ""
"**Fetch any store path and rewrite it to a fully content-addressed store "
"path**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:571
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchClosure {\n"
"  fromStore = \"https://cache.nixos.org\";\n"
"  fromPath = /nix/store/nph9br6y2dmciy6q3dj3fwk2brdlr4gh-git-2.33.1;\n"
"  toPath = /nix/store/ldbhlwhh39wha58rm61bkiiwm6j7211j-git-2.33.1;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:579
msgid ""
"This example fetches `/nix/store/r2jd...` from the specified binary cache, "
"and rewrites it into the content-addressed store path `/nix/store/ldbh...`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:583
msgid ""
"Like the previous example, no extra configuration or privileges are required."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:585
msgid ""
"To find out the correct value for `toPath` given a `fromPath`, use [`nix "
"store make-content-addressed`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-make-"
"content-addressed.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:588
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix store make-content-addressed --from https://cache.nixos.org /nix/store/"
"nph9br6y2dmciy6q3dj3fwk2brdlr4gh-git-2.33.1\n"
"rewrote '/nix/store/nph9br6y2dmciy6q3dj3fwk2brdlr4gh-git-2.33.1' to '/nix/"
"store/ldbhlwhh39wha58rm61bkiiwm6j7211j-git-2.33.1'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:593
msgid ""
"Alternatively, set `toPath = \"\"` and find the correct `toPath` in the "
"error message."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:595
msgid "**Fetch an input-addressed store path as is**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:599
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchClosure {\n"
"  fromStore = \"https://cache.nixos.org\";\n"
"  fromPath = /nix/store/nph9br6y2dmciy6q3dj3fwk2brdlr4gh-git-2.33.1;\n"
"  inputAddressed = true;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:607
msgid ""
"It is possible to fetch an [input-addressed store path](../glossary.md#gloss-"
"input-addressed-store-object) and return it as is. However, this is the "
"least preferred way of invoking `fetchClosure`, because it requires that the "
"input-addressed paths are trusted by the Nix configuration."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:610
msgid "**`builtins.storePath`**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:612
msgid ""
"`fetchClosure` is similar to [`builtins.storePath`](#builtins-storePath) in "
"that it allows you to use a previously built store path in a Nix expression. "
"However, `fetchClosure` is more reproducible because it specifies a binary "
"cache from which the path can be fetched. Also, using content-addressed "
"store paths does not require users to configure [`trusted-public-keys`](../"
"command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-trusted-public-keys) to ensure their "
"authenticity."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:623
msgid ""
"Fetch a path from git. _args_ can be a URL, in which case the HEAD of the "
"repo at that URL is fetched. Otherwise, it can be an attribute with the "
"following attributes (all except `url` optional):"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:627 source/language/builtins.md:1284
msgid "`url`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:629
msgid ""
"The [Git URL](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-clone#_git_urls) of the repo. SCP-"
"like syntax is supported, but relative paths are rewritten to absolute ones. "
"For example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:632
msgid "`git@github.com:repo/path` becomes `ssh://git@github.com/repo/path`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:636
msgid "`name` (default: `source`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:638
msgid "The name of the directory the repo should be exported to in the store."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:640
msgid "`rev` (default: _the tip of `ref`_)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:642
msgid ""
"The [Git revision](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-rev-"
"parse#_specifying_revisions) to fetch. This is typically a commit hash."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:647
msgid "`ref` (default: `HEAD`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:649
msgid ""
"The [Git reference](https://git-scm.com/book/en/v2/Git-Internals-Git-"
"References) under which to look for the requested revision. This is often a "
"branch or tag name."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:654 source/language/builtins.md:687
msgid "This option has no effect once `shallow` cloning is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:656
msgid ""
"By default, the `ref` value is prefixed with `refs/heads/`. As of 2.3.0, Nix "
"doesn't prefix `refs/heads/` if `ref` starts with `refs/`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:659
msgid "`submodules` (default: `false`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:661
msgid ""
"A Boolean parameter that specifies whether submodules should be checked out."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:663
msgid "`exportIgnore` (default: `true`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:665
msgid ""
"A Boolean parameter that specifies whether `export-ignore` from "
"`.gitattributes` should be applied. This approximates part of the `git "
"archive` behavior."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:668
msgid ""
"Enabling this option is not recommended because it is unknown whether the "
"Git developers commit to the reproducibility of `export-ignore` in newer Git "
"versions."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:670
msgid "`shallow` (default: `false`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:672 source/language/builtins.md:1072
msgid ""
"Make a shallow clone when fetching the Git tree. When this is enabled, the "
"options `ref` and `allRefs` have no effect anymore."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:675
msgid "`lfs` (default: `false`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:677
msgid ""
"A boolean that when `true` specifies that [Git LFS](https://git-lfs.com/) "
"files should be fetched."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:681
msgid "`allRefs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:683
msgid ""
"Whether to fetch all references (eg. branches and tags) of the repository. "
"With this argument being true, it's possible to load a `rev` from _any_ "
"`ref`. (by default only `rev`s from the specified `ref` are supported)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:689
msgid ""
"`verifyCommit` (default: `true` if `publicKey` or `publicKeys` are provided, "
"otherwise `false`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:691
msgid ""
"Whether to check `rev` for a signature matching `publicKey` or `publicKeys`. "
"If `verifyCommit` is enabled, then `fetchGit` cannot use a local repository "
"with uncommitted changes. Requires the [`verified-fetches` experimental "
"feature](../development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-verified-"
"fetches)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:695
msgid "`publicKey`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:697
msgid ""
"The public key against which `rev` is verified if `verifyCommit` is enabled. "
"Requires the [`verified-fetches` experimental feature](../development/"
"experimental-features.md#xp-feature-verified-fetches)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:700
msgid "`keytype` (default: `\"ssh-ed25519\"`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:702
msgid "The key type of `publicKey`. Possible values:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:704
msgid "`\"ssh-dsa\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:705
msgid "`\"ssh-ecdsa\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:706
msgid "`\"ssh-ecdsa-sk\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:707
msgid "`\"ssh-ed25519\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:708
msgid "`\"ssh-ed25519-sk\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:709
msgid ""
"`\"ssh-rsa\"` Requires the [`verified-fetches` experimental feature](../"
"development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-verified-fetches)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:712
msgid "`publicKeys`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:714
msgid ""
"The public keys against which `rev` is verified if `verifyCommit` is "
"enabled. Must be given as a list of attribute sets with the following form:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:717
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"{\n"
"  key = \"<public key>\";\n"
"  type = \"<key type>\"; # optional, default: \"ssh-ed25519\"\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:724
msgid ""
"Requires the [`verified-fetches` experimental feature](../development/"
"experimental-features.md#xp-feature-verified-fetches)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:726
msgid "Here are some examples of how to use `fetchGit`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:728
msgid "To fetch a private repository over SSH:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:730
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchGit {\n"
"  url = \"git@github.com:my-secret/repository.git\";\n"
"  ref = \"master\";\n"
"  rev = \"adab8b916a45068c044658c4158d81878f9ed1c3\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:738
msgid "To fetch an arbitrary reference:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:740
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchGit {\n"
"  url = \"https://github.com/NixOS/nix.git\";\n"
"  ref = \"refs/heads/0.5-release\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:747
msgid ""
"If the revision you're looking for is in the default branch of the git "
"repository you don't strictly need to specify the branch name in the `ref` "
"attribute."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:751
msgid ""
"However, if the revision you're looking for is in a future branch for the "
"non-default branch you will need to specify the the `ref` attribute as well."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:755
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchGit {\n"
"  url = \"https://github.com/nixos/nix.git\";\n"
"  rev = \"841fcbd04755c7a2865c51c1e2d3b045976b7452\";\n"
"  ref = \"1.11-maintenance\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:765
msgid ""
"It is nice to always specify the branch which a revision belongs to. Without "
"the branch being specified, the fetcher might fail if the default branch "
"changes. Additionally, it can be confusing to try a commit from a non-"
"default branch and see the fetch fail. If the branch is specified the fault "
"is much more obvious."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:772
msgid ""
"If the revision you're looking for is in the default branch of the git "
"repository you may omit the `ref` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:775
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchGit {\n"
"  url = \"https://github.com/nixos/nix.git\";\n"
"  rev = \"841fcbd04755c7a2865c51c1e2d3b045976b7452\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:782
msgid "To fetch a specific tag:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:784
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchGit {\n"
"  url = \"https://github.com/nixos/nix.git\";\n"
"  ref = \"refs/tags/1.9\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:791
msgid "To fetch the latest version of a remote branch:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:793
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchGit {\n"
"  url = \"ssh://git@github.com/nixos/nix.git\";\n"
"  ref = \"master\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:800
msgid "To verify the commit signature:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:802
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchGit {\n"
"  url = \"ssh://git@github.com/nixos/nix.git\";\n"
"  verifyCommit = true;\n"
"  publicKeys = [\n"
"      {\n"
"        type = \"ssh-ed25519\";\n"
"        key = \"AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIArPKULJOid8eS6XETwUjO48/"
"HKBWl7FTCK0Z//fplDi\";\n"
"      }\n"
"  ];\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:815
msgid ""
"Nix refetches the branch according to the [`tarball-ttl`](../command-ref/"
"conf-file.md#conf-tarball-ttl) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:817
msgid ""
"This behavior is disabled in [pure evaluation mode](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-pure-eval)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:819
msgid "To fetch the content of a checked-out work directory:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:825
msgid ""
"If the URL points to a local directory, and no `ref` or `rev` is given, "
"`fetchGit` uses the current content of the checked-out files, even if they "
"are not committed or added to Git's index. It only considers files added to "
"the Git repository, as listed by `git ls-files`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:837
msgid ""
"Download the specified URL, unpack it and return the path of the unpacked "
"tree. The file must be a tape archive (`.tar`) compressed with `gzip`, "
"`bzip2` or `xz`. If the tarball consists of a single directory, then the top-"
"level path component of the files in the tarball is removed. The typical use "
"of the function is to obtain external Nix expression dependencies, such as a "
"particular version of Nixpkgs, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:845
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"with import (fetchTarball https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/archive/"
"nixos-14.12.tar.gz) {};\n"
"\n"
"stdenv.mkDerivation { … }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:851
msgid ""
"The fetched tarball is cached for a certain amount of time (1 hour by "
"default) in `~/.cache/nix/tarballs/`. You can change the cache timeout "
"either on the command line with `--tarball-ttl` _number-of-seconds_ or in "
"the Nix configuration file by adding the line `tarball-ttl = ` _number-of-"
"seconds_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:857
msgid ""
"Note that when obtaining the hash with `nix-prefetch-url` the option `--"
"unpack` is required."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:860
msgid ""
"This function can also verify the contents against a hash. In that case, the "
"function takes a set instead of a URL. The set requires the attribute `url` "
"and the attribute `sha256`, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:864
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"with import (fetchTarball {\n"
"  url = \"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/archive/nixos-14.12.tar.gz\";\n"
"  sha256 = \"1jppksrfvbk5ypiqdz4cddxdl8z6zyzdb2srq8fcffr327ld5jj2\";\n"
"}) {};\n"
"\n"
"stdenv.mkDerivation { … }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:873 source/language/builtins.md:1293
msgid ""
"Not available in [restricted evaluation mode](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-restrict-eval)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:884
msgid ""
"This function is only available if the [`fetch-tree` experimental feature]"
"(../development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-fetch-tree) is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:892
msgid ""
"Fetch a file system tree or a plain file using one of the supported backends "
"and return an attribute set with:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:894
msgid "the resulting fixed-output [store path](../store/store-path.md)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:895
msgid ""
"the corresponding [NAR](../store/file-system-object/content-"
"address.md#serial-nix-archive) hash"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:896
msgid ""
"backend-specific metadata (currently not documented). <!-- TODO: document "
"output attributes -->"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:898
msgid "_input_ must be an attribute set with the following attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:900
msgid "`type` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:902
msgid ""
"One of the [supported source types](#source-types). This determines other "
"required and allowed input attributes."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:905
msgid "`narHash` (String, optional)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:907
msgid ""
"The `narHash` parameter can be used to substitute the source of the tree. It "
"also allows for verification of tree contents that may not be provided by "
"the underlying transfer mechanism. If `narHash` is set, the source is first "
"looked up is the Nix store and [substituters](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-substituters), and only fetched if not available."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:911
msgid ""
"A subset of the output attributes of `fetchTree` can be re-used for "
"subsequent calls to `fetchTree` to produce the same result again. That is, "
"`fetchTree` is idempotent."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:914
msgid ""
"Downloads are cached in `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/nix`. The remote source is fetched "
"from the network if both are true:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:916
msgid ""
"A NAR hash is supplied and the corresponding store path is not [valid](../"
"glossary.md#gloss-validity), that is, not available in the store"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:920
msgid ""
"[Substituters](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-substituters) are not used "
"in fetching."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:922
msgid ""
"There is no cache entry or the cache entry is older than [`tarball-ttl`](../"
"command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-tarball-ttl)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:924
msgid "Source types"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:926
msgid ""
"The following source types and associated input attributes are supported."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:932
msgid "`\"file\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:935
msgid ""
"Place a plain file into the Nix store. This is similar to "
"[`builtins.fetchurl`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-fetchurl)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:939 source/language/builtins.md:1111
#: source/language/builtins.md:1129 source/language/builtins.md:1169
#: source/language/builtins.md:1183 source/language/builtins.md:1204
msgid "`lastModified` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:941 source/language/builtins.md:1034
#: source/language/builtins.md:1145 source/language/builtins.md:1206
msgid "`name` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:943 source/language/builtins.md:1036
#: source/language/builtins.md:1113 source/language/builtins.md:1131
#: source/language/builtins.md:1147 source/language/builtins.md:1161
#: source/language/builtins.md:1171 source/language/builtins.md:1185
#: source/language/builtins.md:1208
msgid "`narHash` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:945 source/language/builtins.md:1121
#: source/language/builtins.md:1139 source/language/builtins.md:1151
#: source/language/builtins.md:1165 source/language/builtins.md:1175
#: source/language/builtins.md:1193 source/language/builtins.md:1210
msgid "`rev` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:947 source/language/builtins.md:1153
#: source/language/builtins.md:1177 source/language/builtins.md:1212
msgid "`revCount` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:949 source/language/builtins.md:1214
msgid "`unpack` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:951 source/language/builtins.md:1086
#: source/language/builtins.md:1155 source/language/builtins.md:1216
msgid "`url` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:954
msgid "Supported protocols:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:956
msgid "`https`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:960
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"fetchTree {\n"
"  type = \"file\";\n"
"  url = \"https://example.com/index.html\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:967
msgid "`http`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:969
msgid "Insecure HTTP transfer for legacy sources."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:971 source/language/builtins.md:1313
#: source/language/builtins.md:2791
msgid "**Warning**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:973
msgid ""
"HTTP performs no encryption or authentication. Use a `narHash` known in "
"advance to ensure the output has expected contents."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:976
msgid "`file`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:978
msgid "A file on the local file system."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:982
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"fetchTree {\n"
"  type = \"file\";\n"
"  url = \"file:///home/eelco/nix/README.md\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:990
msgid "`\"git\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:993
msgid ""
"Fetch a Git tree and copy it to the Nix store. This is similar to "
"[`builtins.fetchGit`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-fetchGit)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:997
msgid "`allRefs` (Bool, optional)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1000 source/language/builtins.md:1045
msgid ""
"By default, this has no effect. This becomes relevant only once `shallow` "
"cloning is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1002
msgid ""
"Whether to fetch all references (eg. branches and tags) of the repository. "
"With this argument being true, it's possible to load a `rev` from _any_ "
"`ref`. (Without setting this option, only `rev`s from the specified `ref` "
"are supported)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1006 source/language/builtins.md:1031
#: source/language/builtins.md:1083
msgid "Default: `false`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1009
msgid "`dirtyRev` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1011
msgid "`dirtyShortRev` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1013
msgid "`exportIgnore` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1015
msgid "`keytype` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1017
msgid "`lastModified` (Integer, optional)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1020
msgid "Unix timestamp of the fetched commit."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1022 source/language/builtins.md:1065
msgid ""
"If set, pass through the value to the output attribute set. Otherwise, "
"generated from the fetched Git tree."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1026
msgid "`lfs` (Bool, optional)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1029
msgid "Fetch any [Git LFS](https://git-lfs.com/) files."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1038
msgid "`publicKey` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1040
msgid "`publicKeys` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1042
msgid "`ref` (String, optional)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1047
msgid ""
"A [Git reference](https://git-scm.com/book/en/v2/Git-Internals-Git-"
"References), such as a branch or tag name."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1049
msgid "Default: `\"HEAD\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1052
msgid "`rev` (String, optional)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1055
msgid "A Git revision; a commit hash."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1057
msgid "Default: the tip of `ref`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1060
msgid "`revCount` (Integer, optional)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1063
msgid ""
"Number of revisions in the history of the Git repository before the fetched "
"commit."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1069
msgid "`shallow` (Bool, optional)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1075
msgid "Default: `true`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1078
msgid "`submodules` (Bool, optional)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1081
msgid "Also fetch submodules if available."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1089
msgid "The URL formats supported are the same as for Git itself."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1093
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"fetchTree {\n"
"  type = \"git\";\n"
"  url = \"git@github.com:NixOS/nixpkgs.git\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1102
msgid ""
"If the URL points to a local directory, and no `ref` or `rev` is given, Nix "
"only considers files added to the Git index, as listed by `git ls-files` but "
"uses the _current file contents_ of the Git working directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1105
msgid "`verifyCommit` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1107 source/language/builtins.md:1232
msgid "`\"github\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1109 source/language/builtins.md:1127
#: source/language/builtins.md:1181
msgid "`host` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1115 source/language/builtins.md:1133
#: source/language/builtins.md:1187
msgid "`owner` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1117 source/language/builtins.md:1135
#: source/language/builtins.md:1149 source/language/builtins.md:1163
#: source/language/builtins.md:1189
msgid "`ref` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1119 source/language/builtins.md:1137
#: source/language/builtins.md:1191
msgid "`repo` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1123 source/language/builtins.md:1141
#: source/language/builtins.md:1195
msgid "`treeHash` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1125 source/language/builtins.md:1233
msgid "`\"gitlab\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1143
msgid "`\"hg\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1157
msgid "`\"indirect\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1159
msgid "`id` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1167 source/language/builtins.md:1231
msgid "`\"path\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1173
msgid "`path` (String, required)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1179 source/language/builtins.md:1234
msgid "`\"sourcehut\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1197
msgid "`\"tarball\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1200
msgid ""
"Download a tar archive and extract it into the Nix store. This has the same "
"underlying implementation as [`builtins.fetchTarball`](../language/"
"builtins.md#builtins-fetchTarball)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1221
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"fetchTree {\n"
"  type = \"tarball\";\n"
"  url = \"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/tarball/nixpkgs-23.11\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1229
msgid "The following input types are still subject to change:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1235
msgid "`\"mercurial\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1237
msgid ""
"_input_ can also be a [URL-like reference](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-"
"flake.md#flake-references). The additional input types and the URL-like "
"syntax requires the [`flakes` experimental feature](../development/"
"experimental-features.md#xp-feature-flakes) to be enabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1242
msgid "Fetch a GitHub repository using the attribute set representation:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1244
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchTree {\n"
"  type = \"github\";\n"
"  owner = \"NixOS\";\n"
"  repo = \"nixpkgs\";\n"
"  rev = \"ae2e6b3958682513d28f7d633734571fb18285dd\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1253
msgid "This evaluates to the following attribute set:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1255
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"{\n"
"  lastModified = 1686503798;\n"
"  lastModifiedDate = \"20230611171638\";\n"
"  narHash = \"sha256-rA9RqKP9OlBrgGCPvfd5HVAXDOy8k2SmPtB/ijShNXc=\";\n"
"  outPath = \"/nix/store/l5m6qlvfs9sdw14ja3qbzpglcjlb6j1x-source\";\n"
"  rev = \"ae2e6b3958682513d28f7d633734571fb18285dd\";\n"
"  shortRev = \"ae2e6b3\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1268
msgid "Fetch the same GitHub repository using the URL-like syntax:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1270
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchTree \"github:NixOS/nixpkgs/"
"ae2e6b3958682513d28f7d633734571fb18285dd\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1281
msgid ""
"Download the specified URL and return the path of the downloaded file. `arg` "
"can be either a string denoting the URL, or an attribute set with the "
"following attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1286
msgid "The URL of the file to download."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1288
msgid "`name` (default: the last path component of the URL)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1290
msgid ""
"A name for the file in the store. This can be useful if the URL has any "
"characters that are invalid for the store."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1302
msgid ""
"Return a list consisting of the elements of _list_ for which the function "
"_f_ returns `true`. Has linear time complexity in the size of the input "
"_list_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1315
msgid ""
"`filterSource` should not be used to filter store paths. Since "
"`filterSource` uses the name of the input directory while naming the output "
"directory, doing so produces a directory name in the form of `<hash2>-<hash>-"
"<name>`, where `<hash>-<name>` is the name of the input directory. Since "
"`<hash>` depends on the unfiltered directory, the name of the output "
"directory indirectly depends on files that are filtered out by the function. "
"This triggers a rebuild even when a filtered out file is changed. Use "
"`builtins.path` instead, which allows specifying the name of the output "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1326
msgid ""
"This function allows you to copy sources into the Nix store while filtering "
"certain files. For instance, suppose that you want to use the directory "
"`source-dir` as an input to a Nix expression, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1337
msgid ""
"However, if `source-dir` is a Subversion working copy, then all of those "
"annoying `.svn` subdirectories are also copied to the store. Worse, the "
"contents of those directories may change a lot, causing lots of spurious "
"rebuilds. With `filterSource` you can filter out the `.svn` directories:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1343
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"src = builtins.filterSource\n"
"  (path: type: type != \"directory\" || baseNameOf path != \".svn\")\n"
"  ./source-dir;\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1349
msgid ""
"Thus, the first argument _e1_ must be a predicate function that is called "
"for each regular file, directory or symlink in the source tree _e2_. If the "
"function returns `true`, the file is copied to the Nix store, otherwise it "
"is omitted. The function is called with two arguments. The first is the full "
"path of the file. The second is a string that identifies the type of the "
"file, which is either `\"regular\"`, `\"directory\"`, `\"symlink\"` or "
"`\"unknown\"` (for other kinds of files such as device nodes or fifos — but "
"note that those cannot be copied to the Nix store, so if the predicate "
"returns `true` for them, the copy fails). If you exclude a directory, the "
"entire corresponding subtree of _e2_ is excluded."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1368
msgid "Find _lookup-path_ in _search-path_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1370
msgid ""
"[Lookup path](../language/constructs/lookup-path.md) expressions are "
"[desugared](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syntactic_sugar) using this and "
"[`builtins.nixPath`](#builtins-nixPath):"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1376 source/language/builtins.md:2240
msgid "is equivalent to:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1378 source/language/builtins.md:2242
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.findFile builtins.nixPath \"nixpkgs\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1382
msgid ""
"A search path is represented as a list of [attribute sets](./types.md#type-"
"attrs) with two attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1383
msgid "`prefix` is a relative path."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1384
msgid "`path` denotes a file system location"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1386
msgid "Examples of search path attribute sets:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1388
msgid ""
"```\n"
"{\n"
"  prefix = \"\";\n"
"  path = \"/nix/var/nix/profiles/per-user/root/channels\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1394
msgid ""
"```\n"
"{\n"
"  prefix = \"nixos-config\";\n"
"  path = \"/etc/nixos/configuration.nix\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1400
msgid ""
"```\n"
"{\n"
"  prefix = \"nixpkgs\";\n"
"  path = \"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/tarballs/master\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1406 source/language/builtins.md:1456
msgid ""
"```\n"
"{\n"
"  prefix = \"nixpkgs\";\n"
"  path = \"channel:nixpkgs-unstable\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1412
msgid ""
"```\n"
"{\n"
"  prefix = \"flake-compat\";\n"
"  path = \"flake:github:edolstra/flake-compat\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1419
msgid ""
"The lookup algorithm checks each entry until a match is found, returning a "
"[path value](../language/types.md#type-path) of the match:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1421
msgid ""
"If a prefix of `lookup-path` matches `prefix`, then the remainder of _lookup-"
"path_ (the \"suffix\") is searched for within the directory denoted by "
"`path`. The contents of `path` may need to be downloaded at this point to "
"look inside."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1424
msgid ""
"If the suffix is found inside that directory, then the entry is a match. The "
"combined absolute path of the directory (now downloaded if need be) and the "
"suffix is returned."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1429
msgid "A _search-path_ value"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1431
msgid ""
"```\n"
"[\n"
"  {\n"
"    prefix = \"\";\n"
"    path = \"/home/eelco/Dev\";\n"
"  }\n"
"  {\n"
"    prefix = \"nixos-config\";\n"
"    path = \"/etc/nixos\";\n"
"  }\n"
"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1444
msgid ""
"and a _lookup-path_ value `\"nixos-config\"` causes Nix to try `/home/eelco/"
"Dev/nixos-config` and `/etc/nixos` in that order and return the first path "
"that exists."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1446
msgid ""
"If `path` starts with `http://` or `https://`, it is interpreted as the URL "
"of a tarball to be downloaded and unpacked to a temporary location. The "
"tarball must consist of a single top-level directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1449
msgid ""
"The URLs of the tarballs from the official `nixos.org` channels can be "
"abbreviated as `channel:<channel-name>`. See [documentation on `nix-channel`]"
"(../command-ref/nix-channel.md) for details about channels."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1454
msgid "These two search path entries are equivalent:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1462
msgid ""
"```\n"
"{\n"
"  prefix = \"nixpkgs\";\n"
"  path = \"https://channels.nixos.org/nixos-unstable/nixexprs.tar.xz\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1469
msgid ""
"Search paths can also point to source trees using [flake URLs](../command-"
"ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md#url-like-syntax)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1473
msgid "The search path entry"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1475
msgid ""
"```\n"
"{\n"
"  prefix = \"nixpkgs\";\n"
"  path = \"flake:nixpkgs\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1481
msgid ""
"specifies that the prefix `nixpkgs` shall refer to the source tree "
"downloaded from the `nixpkgs` entry in the flake registry."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1483
msgid "Similarly"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1485
msgid ""
"```\n"
"{\n"
"  prefix = \"nixpkgs\";\n"
"  path = \"flake:github:nixos/nixpkgs/nixos-22.05\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1492
msgid ""
"makes `<nixpkgs>` refer to a particular branch of the `NixOS/nixpkgs` "
"repository on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1503 source/language/builtins.md:1780
#: source/language/builtins.md:2347
msgid ""
"This function is only available if the [`flakes` experimental feature](../"
"development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-flakes) is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1511
msgid "Convert a flake reference from attribute set format to URL format."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1513 source/language/builtins.md:2357
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1515
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.flakeRefToString {\n"
"  dir = \"lib\"; owner = \"NixOS\"; ref = \"23.05\"; repo = \"nixpkgs\"; "
"type = \"github\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1521 source/language/builtins.md:1709
#: source/language/builtins.md:1748 source/language/builtins.md:1820
#: source/language/builtins.md:2122 source/language/builtins.md:2386
#: source/language/builtins.md:3205
msgid "evaluates to"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1523
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"\"github:NixOS/nixpkgs/23.05?dir=lib\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1534
msgid ""
"Rounds and converts _number_ to the next lower NixInt value if possible, "
"i.e. `floor *number* <= *number*` and `*number* - floor *number* < 1`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1537
msgid ""
"An evaluation error is thrown, if there exists no such NixInt value `floor "
"*number*`. Due to bugs in previous Nix versions an evaluation error might be "
"thrown, if the datatype of _number_ is a NixInt and if `*number* < "
"-9007199254740992` or `*number* > 9007199254740992`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1541
msgid ""
"If the datatype of _number_ is neither a NixInt (signed 64-bit integer) nor "
"a NixFloat (IEEE-754 double-precision floating-point number), an evaluation "
"error will be thrown."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1551
msgid "Reduce a list by applying a binary operator, from left to right, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1569
msgid ""
"For example, `foldl' (acc: elem: acc + elem) 0 [1 2 3]` evaluates to `6` and "
"`foldl' (acc: elem: { \"${elem}\" = elem; } // acc) {} [\"a\" \"b\"]` "
"evaluates to `{ a = \"a\"; b = \"b\"; }`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1573
msgid ""
"The first argument of `op` is the accumulator whereas the second argument is "
"the current element being processed."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1576
msgid ""
"The return value of each application of `op` is evaluated immediately, even "
"for intermediate values. This way, `foldl'` can operate in constant stack "
"space, allowing it to operate on large lists, regardless of [max-call-depth]"
"(../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-max-call-depth)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1581
msgid ""
"Conventionally, a fold function without the `'` (\"prime\") preserves "
"laziness, but lacks these benefits. See also [Nixpkgs `lib.foldl`](https://"
"nixos.org/manual/nixpkgs/unstable/#function-library-lib.lists.foldl)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1585
msgid "Has linear time complexity in the size of the list."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1594
msgid "Convert a JSON string to a Nix value. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1596
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fromJSON ''{\"x\": [1, 2, 3], \"y\": null}''\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1600
msgid "returns the value `{ x = [ 1 2 3 ]; y = null; }`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1609
msgid "Convert a TOML string to a Nix value. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1611
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fromTOML ''\n"
"  x=1\n"
"  s=\"a\"\n"
"  [table]\n"
"  y=2\n"
"''\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1620
msgid "returns the value `{ s = \"a\"; table = { y = 2; }; x = 1; }`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1629
msgid ""
"Return a set containing the names of the formal arguments expected by the "
"function _f_. The value of each attribute is a Boolean denoting whether the "
"corresponding argument has a default value. For instance, `functionArgs "
"({ x, y ? 123}: ...) = { x = false; y = true; }`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1635
msgid ""
"\"Formal argument\" here refers to the attributes pattern-matched by the "
"function. Plain lambdas are not included, e.g. `functionArgs (x: ...) = { }`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1639 source/language/builtins.md:1898
msgid "Has constant time complexity."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1648
msgid ""
"Generate list of size _length_, with each element _i_ equal to the value "
"returned by _generator_ `i`. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1655
msgid "returns the list `[ 0 1 4 9 16 ]`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1657
msgid "Has linear time complexity."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1666
msgid ""
"`builtins.genericClosure` iteratively computes the transitive closure over "
"an arbitrary relation defined by a function."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1668
msgid ""
"It takes _attrset_ with two attributes named `startSet` and `operator`, and "
"returns a list of attribute sets:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1670
msgid "`startSet`: The initial list of attribute sets."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1673
msgid ""
"`operator`: A function that takes an attribute set and returns a list of "
"attribute sets. It defines how each item in the current set is processed and "
"expanded into more items."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1677
msgid ""
"Each attribute set in the list `startSet` and the list returned by "
"`operator` must have an attribute `key`, which must support equality "
"comparison. The value of `key` can be one of the following types:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1680
msgid "[Int](../language/types.md#type-int)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1681
msgid "[Float](../language/types.md#type-float)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1682
msgid "[Boolean](../language/types.md#type-bool)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1683
msgid "[String](../language/types.md#type-string)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1684
msgid "[Path](../language/types.md#type-path)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1685
msgid "[List](../language/types.md#type-list)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1687
msgid ""
"The result is produced by calling the `operator` on each `item` that has not "
"been called yet, including newly added items, until no new items are added. "
"Items are compared by their `key` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1690
msgid "Common usages are:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1692
msgid "Generating unique collections of items, such as dependency graphs."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1693
msgid "Traversing through structures that may contain cycles or loops."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1694
msgid "Processing data structures with complex internal relationships."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1722
msgid ""
"`getAttr` returns the attribute named _s_ from _set_. Evaluation aborts if "
"the attribute doesn’t exist. This is a dynamic version of the `.` operator, "
"since _s_ is an expression rather than an identifier."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1727 source/language/builtins.md:1839
msgid ""
"Has `O(log n)` time complexity, where `n` is number of attributes in the "
"_set_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1736
msgid "Return the string context of _s_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1738
msgid ""
"The string context tracks references to derivations within a string. It is "
"represented as an attribute set of [store derivation](../glossary.md#gloss-"
"store-derivation) paths mapping to output names."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1741
msgid ""
"Using [string interpolation](../language/string-interpolation.md) on a "
"derivation adds that derivation to the string context. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1744
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.getContext \"${derivation { name = \"a\"; builder = \"b\"; system = "
"\"c\"; }}\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1750
msgid ""
"```\n"
"{ \"/nix/store/arhvjaf6zmlyn8vh8fgn55rpwnxq0n7l-a.drv\" = { outputs = "
"[ \"out\" ]; }; }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1761
msgid ""
"`getEnv` returns the value of the environment variable _s_, or an empty "
"string if the variable doesn’t exist. This function should be used with "
"care, as it can introduce all sorts of nasty environment dependencies in "
"your Nix expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1766
msgid ""
"`getEnv` is used in Nix Packages to locate the file `~/.nixpkgs/config.nix`, "
"which contains user-local settings for Nix Packages. (That is, it does a "
"`getEnv \"HOME\"` to locate the user’s home directory.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1788
msgid ""
"Fetch a flake from a flake reference or a path, and return its output "
"attributes and some metadata. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1790
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"(builtins.getFlake \"nix/"
"55bc52401966fbffa525c574c14f67b00bc4fb3a\").packages.x86_64-linux.nix\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1794
msgid ""
"Unless impure evaluation is allowed (`--impure`), the flake reference must "
"be \"locked\", e.g. contain a Git revision or content hash. An example of an "
"unlocked usage is:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1798
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"(builtins.getFlake \"github:edolstra/dwarffs\").rev\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1809
msgid ""
"Groups elements of _list_ together by the string returned from the function "
"_f_ called on each element. It returns an attribute set where each attribute "
"value contains the elements of _list_ that are mapped to the same "
"corresponding attribute name returned by _f_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1814
msgid "For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1816
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.groupBy (builtins.substring 0 1) [\"foo\" \"bar\" \"baz\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1822
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"{ b = [ \"bar\" \"baz\" ]; f = [ \"foo\" ]; }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1826
msgid ""
"Has `O(n log n)` time complexity, where `n` is the size of the input _list_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1835
msgid ""
"`hasAttr` returns `true` if _set_ has an attribute named _s_, and `false` "
"otherwise. This is a dynamic version of the `?` operator, since _s_ is an "
"expression rather than an identifier."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1848
msgid ""
"Return `true` if string _s_ has a non-empty context. The context can be "
"obtained with [`getContext`](#builtins-getContext)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1854
msgid ""
"Many operations require a string context to be empty because they are "
"intended only to work with \"regular\" strings, and also to help users avoid "
"unintentionally loosing track of string context elements. "
"`builtins.hasContext` can help create better domain-specific errors in those "
"case."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1857
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"name: meta:\n"
"\n"
"if builtins.hasContext name\n"
"then throw \"package name cannot contain string context\"\n"
"else { ${name} = meta; }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1872
msgid ""
"Return a base-16 representation of the cryptographic hash of the file at "
"path _p_. The hash algorithm specified by _type_ must be one of `\"md5\"`, "
"`\"sha1\"`, `\"sha256\"` or `\"sha512\"`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1883
msgid ""
"Return a base-16 representation of the cryptographic hash of string _s_. The "
"hash algorithm specified by _type_ must be one of `\"md5\"`, `\"sha1\"`, "
"`\"sha256\"` or `\"sha512\"`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:1894
msgid ""
