#: source/language/builtins.md:2401
msgid ""
"An enrichment of the built-in path type, based on the attributes present in "
"_args_. All are optional except `path`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2404
msgid ""
"path  \n"
"The underlying path."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2407
msgid ""
"name  \n"
"The name of the path when added to the store. This can used to reference "
"paths that have nix-illegal characters in their names, like `@`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2412
msgid ""
"filter  \n"
"A function of the type expected by [`builtins.filterSource`](#builtins-"
"filterSource), with the same semantics."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2416
msgid ""
"recursive  \n"
"When `false`, when `path` is added to the store it is with a [flat hash](../"
"store/file-system-object/content-address.md#serial-flat), rather than a hash "
"of the [NAR serialization](../store/file-system-object/content-"
"address.md#serial-nix-archive) of the file. Thus, `path` must refer to a "
"regular file, not a directory. This allows similar behavior to `fetchurl`. "
"Defaults to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2425
msgid ""
"sha256  \n"
"When provided, this is the expected [content hash](../store/file-system-"
"object/content-address.md) of the path. Evaluation fails if the hash is "
"incorrect, and providing a hash allows `builtins.path` to be used even when "
"the `pure-eval` nix config option is on."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2439
msgid ""
"Return `true` if the path _path_ exists at evaluation time, and `false` "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2449
msgid ""
"Return an [output placeholder string](../store/derivation/index.md#output-"
"placeholder) for the specified _output_ that will be substituted by the "
"corresponding [output path](../glossary.md#gloss-output-path) at build time."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2455
msgid "Typical outputs would be `\"out\"`, `\"bin\"` or `\"dev\"`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2464
msgid ""
"Return the contents of the directory _path_ as a set mapping directory "
"entries to the corresponding file type. For instance, if directory `A` "
"contains a regular file `B` and another directory `C`, then "
"`builtins.readDir ./A` returns the set"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2469
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"{ B = \"regular\"; C = \"directory\"; }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2473
msgid ""
"The possible values for the file type are `\"regular\"`, `\"directory\"`, "
"`\"symlink\"` and `\"unknown\"`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2483
msgid "Return the contents of the file _path_ as a string."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2492
msgid ""
