"`\"directory\"`, `\"regular\"`, `\"symlink\"`, or `\"unknown\"`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2502
msgid ""
"Remove the attributes listed in _list_ from _set_. The attributes don’t have "
"to exist in _set_. For instance,"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2505
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"removeAttrs { x = 1; y = 2; z = 3; } [ \"a\" \"x\" \"z\" ]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2509
msgid "evaluates to `{ y = 2; }`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2511
msgid ""
"Has `O(n + k log k)` time complexity, where `n` is number of attributes in "
"the _set_ and `k` is the size of _list_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2520
msgid ""
"Given string _s_, replace every occurrence of the strings in _from_ with the "
"corresponding string in _to_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2523
msgid ""
"The argument _to_ is lazy, that is, it is only evaluated when its "
"corresponding pattern in _from_ is matched in the string _s_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2527
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.replaceStrings [\"oo\" \"a\"] [\"a\" \"i\"] \"foobar\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2531
msgid "evaluates to `\"fabir\"`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2533
msgid ""
"Has `O(n k)` time complexity, where `n` is the length of _s_ and `k` is the "
"number of replacements."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2542
msgid ""
"Load, parse, and return the Nix expression in the file _path_, with the "
"attributes from _scope_ available as variables in the lexical scope of the "
"imported file."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2544
msgid ""
"This function is similar to [`import`](#builtins-import), but allows you to "
"provide additional variables that will be available in the scope of the "
"imported expression. The _scope_ argument must be an attribute set; each "
"attribute becomes a variable available in the imported file. Built-in "
"functions and values remain accessible unless shadowed by _scope_ attributes."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2550
msgid ""
"Variables from _scope_ shadow built-ins with the same name, allowing you to "
"override built-ins for the imported expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2554
msgid ""
"Unlike [`import`](#builtins-import), `scopedImport` does not memoize "
"evaluation results. While the parsing result may be reused, each call "
"produces a distinct value. This is observable through performance and side "
"effects such as [`builtins.trace`](#builtins-trace)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2564
msgid "Create a file `greet.nix`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2566
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"# greet.nix\n"
"\"${greeting}, ${name}!\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2571
msgid "Import it with additional variables in scope:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2573
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"scopedImport { greeting = \"Hello\"; name = \"World\"; } ./greet.nix\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2577
msgid ""
"    \"Hello, World!\"\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2579
msgid ""
"Evaluation aborts if the file doesn't exist or contains an invalid Nix "
"expression."
