#: source/language/builtins.md:2598
msgid ""
"Return _list_ in sorted order. It repeatedly calls the function _comparator_ "
"with two elements. The comparator should return `true` if the first element "
"is less than the second, and `false` otherwise. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2607
msgid "produces the list `[ 42 77 147 249 483 526 ]`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2609
msgid ""
"This is a stable sort: it preserves the relative order of elements deemed "
"equal by the comparator."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2612
msgid ""
"_comparator_ must impose a strict weak ordering on the set of values in the "
"_list_. This means that for any elements _a_, _b_ and _c_ from the _list_, "
"_comparator_ must satisfy the following relations:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2616
msgid "Transitivity"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2618
msgid ""
"If a is less than b and b is less than c, then it follows that a is less "
"than c."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2624
msgid "Irreflexivity"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2630
msgid "Transitivity of equivalence"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2632
msgid ""
"First, two values a and b are considered equivalent with respect to the "
"comparator if:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2638
msgid "In other words, neither is considered \"less than\" the other."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2640
msgid "Transitivity of equivalence means:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2642
msgid ""
"If a is equivalent to b, and b is equivalent to c, then a must also be "
"equivalent to c."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2651
msgid ""
"If the _comparator_ violates any of these properties, then `builtins.sort` "
"reorders elements in an unspecified manner."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2654
msgid ""
"Runs in `O(n log n)` time on average, where `n` is the size of the _list_. "
"Uses an adaptive sort that exploits existing sorted runs in the input, down "
"to `O(n)` when the list is already sorted."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2664
msgid ""
"Returns a list composed of non matched strings interleaved with the lists of "
"the [extended POSIX regular expression](http://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/"
"9699919799/basedefs/V1_chap09.html#tag_09_04) _regex_ matches of _str_. Each "
"item in the lists of matched sequences is a regex group."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:2670
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.split \"(a)b\" \"abc\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

